  "scaling_note": "At the bounce, R_b^6=48 M^2/mu^4 makes the rotational-to-scalar ratio M-independent: rho_rot/rho_phi = (6pi/32) a*^2 \u2248 0.589 a*^2. Critical spin a*_c = sqrt(32/(6pi)) \u2248 1.30 is super-extremal; all a*<1 sub-extremal Kerr BHs have rho_rot/rho_phi < 0.48. Scalar dominates shear+rotation for all physical spins.",
  "andersson_rendall_reference": "Andersson & Rendall, Commun. Math. Phys. 218 (2001) 479: scalar field with U(1) axisymmetry yields AVTD (quiescent) cosmological singularities when the scalar kinetic energy dominates the 3-curvature; our bound shows this holds for all sub-extremal spins at the bounce neck.",
  "honest_limitations": "For near-extremal a*~0.9 the ratio rho_rot/rho_phi ~0.48 (scalar dominates by ~2x). This still satisfies the AVTD criterion (scalar > total shear+rotation), but a full axisymmetric/Kerr bounce calculation is needed for extremal BHs rather than a perturbative bound. Realistic astrophysical spins (a*~0.1-0.9) are within the bound. The polymer bounce curvature cap mu^4 is the universal regulator."
}